  "question": "Differentiate $$y=(x+3)^2(x+4)^3(x+5)^4$$ with respect to $x$ by logarithmic differentiation.",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "<b>Taking logarithm</b><br>$$\\log y=2\\log(x+3)+3\\log(x+4)+4\\log(x+5).$$<br><b>Differentiation</b><br>$$\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2}{x+3}+\\frac{3}{x+4}+\\frac{4}{x+5}.$$<br><b>Substitution of the original function</b><br>Therefore, $$\\frac{dy}{dx}=(x+3)^2(x+4)^3(x+5)^4\\left(\\frac{2}{x+3}+\\frac{3}{x+4}+\\frac{4}{x+5}\\right).$$",
  "explanation_image": [],
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\frac{dy}{dx}=(x+3)^2(x+4)^3(x+5)^4\\left(\\frac{1}{x+3}+\\frac{1}{x+4}+\\frac{1}{x+5}\\right)$",
    "B": "$\\frac{dy}{dx}=(x+3)^2(x+4)^3(x+5)^4\\left(\\frac{2}{x+3}+\\frac{3}{x+4}+\\frac{4}{x+5}\\right)$",
    "C": "$\\frac{dy}{dx}=2(x+3)+3(x+4)+4(x+5)$",
    "D": "$\\frac{dy}{dx}=(x+3)(x+4)^2(x+5)^3\\left(2+3+4\\right)$"
